l","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located across from the Axinn Library entrance on South Campus. Verify current lab hours and HofstraCard access before planning an overnight session.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hofstra-collaborative-learning-center","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Collaborative Learning Center","title":"Move Group Work to the Second Floor","subtitle":"Second floor of the Joan and Donald E. Axinn Library","notes":"Meet here when a project benefits from conversation and shared work; choose another library area when you need individual quiet.","short_summary":"A library lounge specifically developed for collaborative learning rather than silent solo study.","evidence_claim":"Hofstra lists the Collaborative Learning Center on Axinn Library's second floor as a campus lounge, and its facilities archive says the space was created as a learning center and lounge.","source_url":"https://www.hofstra.edu/facilities-operations/projects-archive.html","source_title":"Construction and Projects Archives | Facilities & Operations | Hofstra University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Second floor of Axinn Library. Access follows current library building hours and University entry policies.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hofstra-axinn-library-tenth-floor","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Axinn Library 10th-Floor Study Space","title":"Match Your Seat to the Assignment","subtitle":"Tenth floor of the Joan and Donald E. Axinn Library","notes":"Choose an individual desk for focused work or use group desks and sofa-style seating when classmates need to collaborate.","short_summary":"A renovated upper-floor study area offering distinct seating modes for solo and collaborative work.","evidence_claim":"Hofstra reports that Axinn Library's renovated 10th floor is a dedicated collaborative and study space with individual and group desks, sofas, and egg chairs.","source_url":"https://news.hofstra.edu/2024/09/23/celebrating-the-librarys-10th-floor-makeover/","source_title":"Celebrating the Library's 10th Floor Renovation | Hofstra University News","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2024-09-23","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Located on Axinn Library's 10th floor. Use is subject to current library hours, building policies, and any event reservations.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hofstra-first-gen-lounge","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"First-Gen Lounge","title":"Connect With First-Generation Support","subtitle":"Room 219 in the Sondra and David S. Mack Student Center","notes":"Stop in for first-generation programming and mentorship, and follow the office's official updates before attending a scheduled activity.","short_summary":"A dedicated lounge where first-generation students can connect with support programs and mentors.","evidence_claim":"Hofstra identifies the First-Gen Lounge in Student Center Room 219 and says First-Generation Support and Engagement provides programming and mentorship.","source_url":"https://www.hofstra.edu/admission/deposit-resources/","source_title":"Deposited Student Resources | Hofstra University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Room 219, Mack Student Center. The official page does not publish regular drop-in hours; confirm access or program timing with First-Generation Support and Engagement.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hofstra-multisport-courts","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Hofstra Multisport Courts","title":"Take a Break on the Outdoor Courts","subtitle":"Beside the Wellness and Campus Living Center on North Campus","notes":"Check whether intramurals are scheduled, then bring classmates for basketball or use available RecRe Box equipment as directed.","short_summary":"Open student recreation courts with basketball facilities and app-accessible shared equipment nearby.","evidence_claim":"Hofstra says the outdoor Multisport Courts are next to the Wellness Center, equipped for basketball, open for student use and intramurals, and served by a RecRe Box with borrowable gear.","source_url":"https://www.hofstra.edu/admission/deposit-resources/","source_title":"Deposited Student Resources | Hofstra University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Outdoor courts next to the Wellness and Campus Living Center on North Campus. Availability may change for intramurals, programs, or weather.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"hofstra-emily-lowe-gallery","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Emily Lowe Gallery","title":"Use the Gallery as a Class Extension","subtitle":"Hofstra University Museum of Art in Emily Lowe Hall","notes":"Visit during current gallery access periods, look closely at the changing exhibition, and use one object to prompt discussion or writing.","short_summary":"A campus museum gallery used for exhibitions, object study, class meetings, and interdisciplinary assignments.","evidence_claim":"The Hofstra University Museum of Art documents class meetings in the Emily Lowe Gallery and says its exhibitions support gallery teaching, tours, and permanent-collection object study.","source_url":"https://www.hofstra.edu/museum/hofstra-faculty.html","source_title":"Museum Education – Hofstra Faculty | Hofstra University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":n